    33	    // never reported the daily limit at all. The cap itself was never exceeded — the claim inside
    34	    // the insert compares `comment_count_date = $today::date` in SQL and is authoritative (M11-1
    35	    // C16) — but an agent at the cap was handed a 429 claiming 50 comments remaining. Casting in
    36	    // SQL makes this pre-check use the same notion of "today" the claim uses, which is the JS UTC
    37	    // day both sides bind. Memory mode always compared two strings and was correct throughout, so
    38	    // this was a db-only divergence.
    39	    const rows = await sql!`
